{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1778866298,"nonce":"mGIefB8uSbZoQtS8/eNnFb3vKTo=","message":"## Clarification: generalized graph view as a first-class Mandible surface\n\nMandible likely needs a generalized graph view, not just conditional provider actions or small graph widgets. The graph should be able to serve as a project-structure and provenance surface across repos, issues, work units, commits, artifacts, provider specs/runs, and curated semantic relationships. This implies UX work around subgraph selection, graph type/mode, filtering, clustering, hover previews, click-through detail panes, and provider-specific actions on compatible nodes.\n\nThis may eventually become a canonical Mandible view that overlaps with existing tabs. For example, issue browsing could remain available as a traditional list/sidebar, but issue relationships and cross-references might also be navigated as a graph with previews and a right-side detail panel. Agents working on Mandible specs should not assume the current Issues/Switchboard/etc. views are final silos; when this becomes relevant, ask MLL about which existing views should remain separate, be collapsed into the graph view, or become alternate projections of the same underlying project graph.\n\nRelated visual-language thread: `cf51a72`. This coordination issue should keep the broader product/architecture concern: the graph view is potentially a central Mandible workspace, not merely decoration around the provider registry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}